      "passageLabel": "Travellers' tips",
      "paragraphs": [
        [
          "culture vultures"
        ],
        [
          "THIS SUMMER the royal ",
          {
            "questionId": "places-1-1"
          },
          " is open to the public for the first time with exhibitions of paintings from across the centuries. There is also a private ",
          {
            "questionId": "places-1-2"
          },
          " in the city with paintings for sale."
        ],
        [
          "FOR LOVERS of architecture, head to the ",
          {
            "questionId": "places-1-3"
          },
          ", with its interesting mix of historic buildings. ",
          {
            "questionId": "places-1-4"
          },
          " in the east of the city, is the site of the old Jewish district. It also has a number of beautiful churches and the city ",
          {
            "questionId": "places-1-5"
          },
          "."
        ],
        [
          "TAKE A TRIP out to the Roman ",
          {
            "questionId": "places-1-6"
          },
          " and learn about some of the first people to live in the area. Local archaeologists give talks at the weekends."
        ],
        [
          "get active"
        ],
        [
          "CHECK OUT SkyFlyer, the tallest roller coaster in the country, at the new ",
          {
            "questionId": "places-1-7"
          },
          ". It's ",
          {
            "questionId": "places-1-8"
          },
          " 45 minutes ",
          {
            "questionId": "places-1-9"
          },
          " the city but it's well worth the trip."
        ],
        [
          "ENJOY the ",
          {
            "questionId": "places-1-10"
          },
          " - there are lots of bars and restaurants and it's always very lively."
        ],
        [
          "For a MORE RELAXING time, take a boat out on the ",
          {
            "questionId": "places-1-11"
          },
          ". Swimming isn't allowed but you can enjoy a picnic down ",
          {
            "questionId": "places-1-12"
          },
          " the water."
        ],
        [
          "fun on a budget"
        ],
        [
          "IF MONEY IS A BIT TIGHT, join a free walking tour. Local residents act as guides and give an insider view of the city. All tours start inside the city ",
          {
            "questionId": "places-1-13"
          },
          " under the clock tower."
        ],
        [
          "DON'T MISS the market on Fridays and Saturdays with ",
          {
            "questionId": "places-1-14"
          },
          " all ",
          {
            "questionId": "places-1-15"
          },
          " the High Street. You'll find everything from cheap and tasty snacks to local souvenirs at bargain prices."
        ]
      ]
    },
